00:25:50.713 --> 00:25:54.642
But there was something I was so such a driven young actor.
但有一点我是一个如此有动力的年轻演员。

00:25:54.642 --> 00:25:57.372
I really knew this was a big opportunity.
我真的知道这是一个很大的机会。

00:25:57.372 --> 00:25:59.237
I really wanted to seize it.
我真的很想抓住它。

00:25:59.237 --> 00:26:01.900
But, you know, I lived in New York City.
但是，你知道，我住在纽约市。

00:26:01.900 --> 00:26:03.898
I drank a lot of beer at bars.
我在酒吧喝了很多啤酒。

00:26:03.898 --> 00:26:09.692
I got scared to talk to women and some nights it worked and some nights it didn't work.
我害怕和女人说话，有些晚上它有效，有些晚上它不起作用。

00:26:09.692 --> 00:26:13.288
You know, like I went to a small liberal arts college.
你知道，就像我上了一所小型文理学院一样。

00:26:13.288 --> 00:26:14.353
I was from Ohio.
我来自俄亥俄州。

00:26:14.353 --> 00:26:18.282
Like there were a lot of biographical things that lined up.
就像有很多传记一样排列在一起。

00:26:18.282 --> 00:26:23.743
But I also think I had, I constitutionally, I think have, I don't know what it is.
但我也认为我有，从本质上讲，我认为有，我不知道那是什么。

00:26:23.743 --> 00:26:29.137
I went on a very spiritual journey when I was in my 30s on, you know, off screen.
当我三十多岁的时候，你知道，在银幕之外，我经历了一次非常精神的旅程。

00:26:29.137 --> 00:26:43.655
And I was really trying to ask myself some big questions because I think what happens to me, and this is something we could talk about later, but like when you have success, you get to the kind of top of that mountain.
我真的很想问自己一些大问题，因为我想我会发生什么，这是我们稍后可以讨论的事情，但就像当你取得成功时，你就会到达山顶。

00:26:43.655 --> 00:26:51.379
It's the thing of like, you climb to the top of the ladder and realize, maybe it was propped against the wrong wall.
这就像，你爬到梯子的顶部，然后意识到，也许它靠在了错误的墙上。

00:26:51.940 --> 00:26:53.717
You know, like, is this what I want?
你知道，这就是我想要的吗？

00:26:53.717 --> 00:26:55.148
Is this what I'm looking for?
这就是我要找的吗？

00:26:55.148 --> 00:26:59.048
And so I really started to ask myself some big questions about, is this enough?
所以我真的开始问自己一些大问题，这足够了吗？

00:26:59.048 --> 00:27:01.220
You know, what do I really want to be doing?
你知道，我真正想做的是什么？

00:27:02.259 --> 00:27:05.128
And maybe those are, you know, not unmosby-ish.
你知道，也许这些并不是unmosby-ish。

00:27:05.128 --> 00:27:10.498
But I think I appreciated his energy and his passion in his optimism and his resilience.
但我想我很欣赏他的精力、热情、乐观和韧性。

00:27:10.498 --> 00:27:20.079
I mean, that would be the biggest thing that I would almost like to learn from him and honor about him was, man, that guy got kicked down and just came back.
我的意思是，这将是我想从他身上学到的最重要的事情，对他的荣誉是，伙计，那个家伙被踢倒了，然后又回来了。

00:27:20.079 --> 00:27:20.872
He came back.
他回来了。

00:27:20.872 --> 00:27:22.825
And that's, that's a great word.
那是，这是一个很棒的词。

00:27:22.825 --> 00:27:23.325
Yeah.
是的。

00:27:23.325 --> 00:27:25.094
Resilience and vulnerability.
韧性和脆弱性。

00:27:24.900 --> 00:27:28.715
You know, he was not, he was not afraid to say how he was feeling.
你知道，他不是，他并不害怕说出自己的感受。

00:27:28.715 --> 00:27:31.547
He was not afraid to, um, well, that's the thing.
他并不害怕，嗯，好吧，就是这样。

00:27:31.547 --> 00:27:33.743
I think it heroic qualities for a man.
我认为这是一个男人的英雄品质。

00:27:33.743 --> 00:27:34.243
I agree.
我同意。

00:27:34.243 --> 00:27:37.191
And I don't think you were seeing that in comedies.
我认为你不会在喜剧中看到这一点。

00:27:37.191 --> 00:27:39.793
It's like you weren't seeing a man sensitive.
就好像你没有看到一个敏感的男人。

00:27:39.793 --> 00:27:42.567
It's like the speech Ted gives after fucking up.
这就像特德在搞砸后发表的演讲。

00:27:42.567 --> 00:27:51.238
After, say, blurting out I love you up in Robbins, you don't get that amazing speech from Ted and so wonderfully acted and performed by you out there.
比如说，在《罗宾斯》中脱口而出“我爱你”之后，你就听不到泰德的精彩演讲，也听不到你在场的精彩表演。

00:27:51.238 --> 00:27:53.608
I mean, that is, that is just a home run.
我的意思是，那只是一个本垒打。

00:27:53.608 --> 00:27:56.151
I was like tears in my eyes rewatching that.
当我重温这一幕时，我的眼里含着泪水。

00:27:56.151 --> 00:27:58.463
In part just because of how good it was.
部分原因只是因为它有多好。

00:27:58.463 --> 00:28:04.937
And in part just remembering being there that night watching you do it on on that street at the CBS Radford Lot.
部分原因只是记得那天晚上在哥伦比亚广播公司雷德福德停车场的那条街上看着你做这件事。

00:28:04.900 --> 00:28:07.740
That was not where we shot, how I met your mother after the pilot.
那不是我们拍摄的地方，也不是我在试播后遇见你母亲的地方。

00:28:07.740 --> 00:28:15.740
We shot the pilot in the valley of the CBS Lot, and then shot every other episode, basically at the Fox Lot in West LA, so it was completely different.
我们在哥伦比亚广播公司的山谷里拍摄了试播集，然后每隔一集都拍摄，基本上是在西洛杉矶的福克斯基地，所以这是完全不同的。

00:28:15.740 --> 00:28:23.140
But for the pilot, for CBS, that's where we had the space and the money sent us there at that moment.
但对于哥伦比亚广播公司的试播集来说，那是我们拥有空间和资金的地方。

00:28:23.140 --> 00:28:28.019
And I had this memory, Josh, of you out there in the magic of that night.
乔什，我在那个神奇的夜晚里记住了你。

00:28:28.019 --> 00:28:32.940
And it was a night shoot on the fake New York City Street, but it looked beautiful.
而且是在假纽约街拍的夜景，不过看起来很美。

00:28:32.940 --> 00:28:34.180
It was all lit up all pretty.
一切都被照亮了，一切都很漂亮。

00:28:34.180 --> 00:28:37.740
The, the, you know, there's that thing where they've kind of went down the sidewalks.
那个，那个，你知道，有一种东西是他们沿着人行道走的。

00:28:37.740 --> 00:28:39.980
So, like listening and shiny and magical.
所以，喜欢聆听，闪亮而神奇。

00:28:39.980 --> 00:28:47.220
And just watching you there, it's like I stepped into that TV now from the year 2025 back into 2005.
光是看着你，就好像我从 2025 年走进了那台电视，回到了 2005 年。

00:28:47.220 --> 00:28:51.740
And I felt I was there with young you and young me.
我感觉我就在年轻的你和年轻的我身边。

00:28:51.740 --> 00:28:56.779
And I had this unbelievable wave of nostalgia that I was like, overcome by.
我有一股难以置信的怀旧之情，我被它征服了。

00:28:56.779 --> 00:28:59.220
And I was like, I wanted to go be with some.
我当时想，我想和一些人在一起。

00:28:59.220 --> 00:29:00.539
I wanted to go be there.
我想去那里。

00:29:00.539 --> 00:29:02.579
I wanted to feel what they felt.
我想感受他们的感受。

00:29:02.579 --> 00:29:11.440
There was this drumming aliveness I felt of like, yes, in our late 20s or 30s, we were 30, I think.
我感觉有一种鼓点般的活力，是的，在我们 20 多岁或 30 多岁的时候，我想我们已经 30 岁了。

00:29:11.440 --> 00:29:14.519
And there we were, this was our first big shot.
就这样，这是我们的第一个大人物。

00:29:14.519 --> 00:29:17.880
And we were all vibing and aligned and connected.
我们都充满活力、团结一致、相互联系。

00:29:17.880 --> 00:29:19.200
We knew what we were doing.
我们知道我们在做什么。

00:29:19.200 --> 00:29:24.799
I remember watching you do that speech, which, again, is so brilliantly performed, brilliantly written.
我记得看着你做那次演讲，演讲再次表现得非常出色，写得也非常出色。

00:29:24.799 --> 00:29:28.799
I give Carter so much, like Carter really wrote, he wrote that speech so beautifully.
我给了卡特很多，就像卡特真正写的那样，他的演讲写得非常漂亮。

00:29:28.799 --> 00:29:30.519
I feel like that's such a Carter.
我感觉这就是卡特。

00:29:30.519 --> 00:29:34.039
That was really Carter connecting with Ted, I think, because the Carter was single.
我认为那确实是卡特与泰德的联系，因为卡特是单身。

00:29:34.039 --> 00:29:35.359
Carter was saying how he felt.
卡特说出了他的感受。

00:29:35.359 --> 00:29:39.880
He wanted to do everything Ted said in that speech is where Carter wanted to be.
他想做特德在那次演讲中所说的一切，这也是卡特想做的。

00:29:39.880 --> 00:29:47.839
It was his same aspiration, and it's very vulnerable to write that, and you just performed it with such vulnerability, but also this kind of heroism.
这是他同样的愿望，而且写起来很脆弱，而你只是表现得如此脆弱，但也有这种英雄主义。

00:29:47.839 --> 00:30:00.880
You forget all about how much Ted fucked up two seconds ago, saying I love you up in the apartment, because now he's your hero, and he's so emotionally articulate and intelligent in that speech that I think he wins you over and you don't get that speech unless Ted fucked up upstairs.
你完全忘记了特德两秒钟前在公寓里搞砸了多少，说我爱你在公寓里，因为现在他是你的英雄，他在那次演讲中情绪表达清晰且聪明，我认为他赢得了你的支持，除非特德在楼上搞砸了，否则你不会得到那个演讲。

00:30:00.880 --> 00:30:11.960
So Ted has to be the guy who can fuck up upstairs and has to be the guy that absolutely sweeps you off your feet by acknowledging the fuck up and then surprising you with this unbelievable sentiment that you did not see coming in that moment.
所以特德必须是那个可以在楼上搞砸的人，并且必须是那个让你彻底震惊的人，他承认搞砸了，然后用你在那一刻没有预见到的令人难以置信的情绪让你感到惊讶。

00:30:11.960 --> 00:30:13.559
So I mean, it works.
所以我的意思是，它有效。

00:30:13.559 --> 00:30:14.400
Yeah.
是的。

00:30:14.400 --> 00:30:17.119
It works so well because Robin gave him the look.
它非常有效，因为罗宾给了他这样的表情。

00:30:17.119 --> 00:30:18.880
She gave him the look.
她看了他一眼。

00:30:18.880 --> 00:30:28.750
And this old man, he must have me I fell in love with you, New York City.
而这个老人，他一定是让我爱上了你，纽约市。

00:30:28.750 --> 00:30:32.359
And now, commercials!
现在，广告！

00:30:32.359 --> 00:30:36.400
Hi, I'm Alex Goldman, host of the HyperFixed Podcast.
大家好，我是 Alex Goldman，HyperFixed 播客的主持人。

00:30:36.400 --> 00:30:40.079
Each week, we take listeners' problems and try to solve them for them.
每周，我们都会收集听众的问题并尝试为他们解决。

00:30:40.079 --> 00:30:43.079
Problems like, I'm 30 and I'm scared to drive in New York.
诸如此类的问题，我已经 30 岁了，我害怕在纽约开车。

00:30:43.079 --> 00:30:46.759
Or, why can't I adjust the volume of my car stereo when I'm in reverse?
或者，为什么我倒车时无法调节汽车音响的音量？

00:30:46.759 --> 00:30:49.319
We also solve non-car related problems.
我们还解决非汽车相关的问题。

00:30:49.319 --> 00:30:55.369
If you have a problem, not only will we fix it, we'll expose the hidden systems that to cause that problem in the first place.
如果您遇到问题，我们不仅会修复它，还会首先暴露导致该问题的隐藏系统。

00:30:55.369 --> 00:30:57.849
That's the HyperFixed Podcast from Radio Topia.
这是来自 Radio Topia 的 HyperFixed 播客。

00:30:57.849 --> 00:31:12.450
Find it wherever you find podcasts or at HyperFixedPod.com.
无论您在哪里找到播客或在 HyperFixedPod.com 上都可以找到它。

00:31:12.450 --> 00:31:15.369
End of commercials back to show.
广告结束返回放映。

00:31:15.369 --> 00:31:20.460
Can I ask both of you how present were you at the time?
我能问一下你们当时在场的情况如何吗？

00:31:20.859 --> 00:31:32.950
I mean, Craig, you would describe to me all of a sudden you go from writer to owner of rather large small business with millions of dollars on the line and you're going all over.
我的意思是，克雷格，你会向我描述一下，你突然从作家变成了相当大的小企业的老板，冒着数百万美元的风险，然后你就一切都结束了。

00:31:32.950 --> 00:31:34.910
were you able to appreciate this in the moment?
此刻你能体会到这一点吗？

00:31:34.910 --> 00:31:37.150
Could you breathe through it and go look what we're doing here?
你能呼吸一下并看看我们在这里做什么吗？

00:31:37.150 --> 00:31:40.269
I think I did because Alec, we didn't know if the show was that, we thought that was it.
我想我这么做是因为亚历克，我们不知道这部剧是不是那样，我们认为就是这样。

00:31:40.269 --> 00:31:43.430
We were shooting a pilot and we were like, I can't believe we got it this far.
我们当时正在拍摄一名试播集，我们当时想，我不敢相信我们能走到这一步。

00:31:43.430 --> 00:31:45.309
We'll be able to show this to our friends.
我们将能够向我们的朋友展示这个。

00:31:45.309 --> 00:31:52.670
I mean, I did have this feeling that something was magical about like a moment like watching Josh chew that speech on that location chewed outside on the New York Street.
我的意思是，我确实有一种感觉，有一种神奇的感觉，就像看着乔什在纽约街上咀嚼那篇演讲的那一刻一样。

00:31:52.670 --> 00:31:55.349
Like I had the feeling like this is gonna go.
就像我有一种感觉，这件事就要过去了。

00:31:55.349 --> 00:32:00.069
But you don't know, it was just like, let's make this one good episode and we'll see if it ever goes in there.
但你不知道，就像是，让我们把这一集打造成精彩的一集，然后看看它是否会出现在那里。

00:32:00.069 --> 00:32:02.990
probably it won't, the odds are against you, way against you.
也许不会，机会对你不利，完全对你不利。

00:32:02.990 --> 00:32:06.150
So I didn't yet feel that we're running a big business.
所以我还没有感觉到我们正在经营一家大企业。

00:32:06.150 --> 00:32:14.230
I was like, we have this amount of money and this number of days and these actors, let's make the best 22-minute show we can.
我当时想，我们有这么多的钱、这么多的天数和这些演员，让我们尽力制作最好的 22 分钟节目吧。

00:32:14.230 --> 00:32:16.029
And it felt very fleeting.
这感觉非常短暂。

00:32:16.029 --> 00:32:17.470
And maybe that was part of its magic.
也许这就是它的魔力的一部分。

00:32:17.470 --> 00:32:19.150
It felt absolutely fleeting.
感觉绝对是转瞬即逝的。

00:32:19.150 --> 00:32:27.710
In that way, it felt very innocent because you look back now and you're like, well, of course, we know now they're gonna do 208 episodes of this 207 more.
这样一来，感觉非常无辜，因为你现在回头看，你会想，好吧，当然，我们现在知道他们会再拍 207 集中的 208 集。

00:32:27.710 --> 00:32:32.190
But at the time, we were just trying to make a good show that would get the attention of the network and that would put us on the air.
但当时，我们只是想制作一个好的节目来引起网络的关注，从而让我们播出。

00:32:32.190 --> 00:32:33.349
One good episode, yeah.
不错的一集，嗯。

00:32:33.349 --> 00:32:34.549
One good episode, right?
很好的一集，对吧？

00:32:34.549 --> 00:32:35.390
One good one.
一件好事。

00:32:35.390 --> 00:32:40.430
And then we, and another thing I loved watching it, just to tick off some more things that jumped out of me watching it.
然后我们，还有另一件事我喜欢看它，只是为了勾选更多我在观看它时跳出来的东西。

00:32:40.430 --> 00:32:43.750
And then I'm dying to hear more about what it was like watching with Jordana, I really am.
然后我很想听到更多关于和乔丹娜一起观看比赛的感觉，我真的很想知道。

00:32:43.750 --> 00:32:45.589
I know we were saving that made from the end.
我知道我们正在保存最后制作的东西。

00:32:45.589 --> 00:32:46.990
Just, I'm just so curious.
只是，我实在是太好奇了。

00:32:48.349 --> 00:32:51.710
But you know what, I loved how everything was important.
但你知道吗，我喜欢一切都很重要。

00:32:51.710 --> 00:32:53.230
Everything was important right away.
一切立刻就变得重要了。

00:32:53.230 --> 00:32:57.190
The whole episode begins with Marshall changed my whole world.
整集从马歇尔改变了我的整个世界开始。

00:32:57.190 --> 00:33:00.198
He changed the game, he screwed everything up getting engaged.
他改变了游戏规则，他订婚了，把一切都搞砸了。

00:33:00.198 --> 00:33:01.071
That's a big deal.
这是一件大事。

00:33:01.071 --> 00:33:02.478
Your best friend got engaged.
你最好的朋友订婚了。

00:33:02.478 --> 00:33:05.050
So Ted decides I'm going to meet the love of my life.
所以特德决定我要去见我一生的挚爱。

00:33:05.050 --> 00:33:07.670
And all these important things start happening, right?
所有这些重要的事情都开始发生，对吗？

00:33:07.670 --> 00:33:10.047
And all these, like everything feels high stakes.
所有这些，就像所有事情都感觉风险很大。

00:33:10.047 --> 00:33:11.843
It all takes place in this one night.
这一切都发生在这一晚。

00:33:11.843 --> 00:33:15.142
I love all the time jumps, but the stakes of the show are one night.
我喜欢所有的时间跳跃，但演出的赌注是一晚。

00:33:15.142 --> 00:33:21.401
And I love that in the background of this and raising the stakes in this weird kind of stealthy way that people might not notice.
我喜欢在这种背景下以人们可能不会注意到的奇怪的隐秘方式提高赌注。

00:33:21.401 --> 00:33:25.428
There's a guy on a bridge who's going to jump off the bridge in Robin's news story.
在罗宾的新闻报道中，桥上有一个人要跳桥。

00:33:25.428 --> 00:33:56.869
And I think it's so important to the pilot that there's this life or death tension just ticking this little clock ticking in the background is that guy gonna jump off that bridge and how that sort of factors back into like the moment Ted you know the the moment in the bar where they want they see that he didn't jump and Marshall says he didn't jump which first of all I felt relief I was like oh thank god that guy didn't jump right guys just like back into it and it's just like that idea of these high stakes and it's all life or death this is our life this is our life right now tonight can is going to be a story Are we gonna be tall forever?
我认为对飞行员来说非常重要的是，这种生死攸关的紧张气氛只是在背景中滴答作响的小时钟滴答作响，那家伙要从桥上跳下来，以及这种因素如何回到像泰德你知道酒吧里他们希望他们看到他没有跳的那一刻，马歇尔说他没有跳，首先我感到宽慰，我就像哦，感谢上帝，那家伙没有跳到正确的位置，就像回到它一样，就像这些想法一样高风险，生死攸关，这就是我们的生活，今晚这就是我们的生活，这将是一个故事我们会永远高大吗？

00:33:56.869 --> 00:33:57.710
Are we gonna live?
我们还能活下去吗？

00:33:57.710 --> 00:33:58.549
Are we gonna die?
我们会死吗？

00:33:58.549 --> 00:33:59.390
Are we gonna take the leap?
我们要迈出这一步吗？

00:33:59.390 --> 00:34:00.230
Are we gonna not take the leap?
我们不打算迈出这一步吗？

00:34:00.230 --> 00:34:01.750
Is taking the leap good or bad?
飞跃是好是坏？

00:34:01.750 --> 00:34:03.430
Ted is a great joke about that.
特德对此开了一个很大的玩笑。

00:34:03.430 --> 00:34:09.230
And, but boy, I just, I loved how everything felt like the most important thing in the world in that part.
而且，但是天哪，我只是，我喜欢那部分的一切感觉都是世界上最重要的事情。

00:34:09.230 --> 00:34:12.309
What is it in the van that pulls up is we gotta jumper.
停在车里的东西是我们得跳伞。

