Where have they come to the restaurant?
他们到哪儿来的餐厅？

00:34:24.309 --> 00:34:27.349
How did they know that there weren't trackers on our phones yet?
他们怎么知道我们的手机上还没有追踪器？

00:34:27.349 --> 00:34:31.750
Greg, you pointed out that you didn't know if there would be more than one episode.
格雷格，你指出你不知道是否会有不止一集。

00:34:31.750 --> 00:34:32.750
This was what you were doing.
这就是你正在做的事情。

00:34:32.750 --> 00:34:33.750
You sort of put your all into it.
你几乎投入了全部。

00:34:33.750 --> 00:34:41.269
I think nothing that shows out in this pilot very much show is yes, it launches a series the way a great pilot launches.
我认为在这个试播节目中没有什么表现出来的是肯定的，它像一个伟大的试播节目一样推出了一系列节目。

00:34:41.269 --> 00:34:44.750
It's also just a great romantic comedy in 22 minutes.
这也是一部22分钟的精彩浪漫喜剧。

00:34:44.750 --> 00:34:54.269
You kind of have a whole movie happening in here and like you're saying because everything is so important, it has that cinematic feel and it's got that story going on.
就像你说的，一整部电影都在这里发生，因为一切都很重要，它有电影的感觉，而且故事还在继续。

00:34:54.269 --> 00:34:58.308
the background and it has this romantic lead going through quite a bit.
背景和浪漫的主角经历了相当多的时间。

00:34:58.308 --> 00:35:03.825
You just happen to end this romantic story with not getting the girl instead of getting the girl.
你只是碰巧以没有得到女孩而不是得到女孩来结束这个浪漫的故事。

00:35:03.825 --> 00:35:04.325
Yeah.
是的。

00:35:04.110 --> 00:35:08.034
But it really felt like you piled in a full tail in here.
但真的感觉就像你在这里堆满了尾巴。

00:35:08.034 --> 00:35:11.409
I think that's why it gets a lot done in a hurry.
我认为这就是为什么它会匆忙完成很多工作。

00:35:11.409 --> 00:35:13.474
It gets a lot done in a hurry.
很快就能完成很多事情。

00:35:13.474 --> 00:35:15.196
I was also proud of that.
我也为此感到自豪。

00:35:15.196 --> 00:35:20.705
By the end of act one, I made a little note to myself like so much has happened.
在第一幕结束时，我给自己做了一个小记录，就像发生了很多事情一样。

00:35:20.705 --> 00:35:22.908
So much has happened in act one.
第一幕发生了很多事情。

00:35:22.908 --> 00:35:27.659
It's like you You know so much very quickly and so much has happened.
就像你一样，你很快就知道了很多，也发生了很多事情。

00:35:27.659 --> 00:35:28.940
I also loved another little moment.
我也喜欢另一个小时刻。

00:35:28.940 --> 00:35:40.699
I love that Robin's friend in the corner going, what's taking so long, you know, calling out because the show kind of like, it's just a hilarious thing to look back at and go, little did we know how it's going to be 208 episodes.
我喜欢罗宾的朋友在角落里走来走去，什么花了这么长时间，你知道，大声喊叫，因为这部剧有点像，回顾过去真是一件很搞笑的事情，我们几乎不知道这会是 208 集。

00:35:40.699 --> 00:35:43.019
That woman though, that was the truest line in the whole pilot.
但那个女人，却是整部试播集里最真实的台词。

00:35:43.019 --> 00:35:50.780
It was the woman who goes, what's taking so long, because the whole thing was going to take longer than anyone ever thought and we brought her back and you're the end of the show.
是那个女人走了，什么花了这么长时间，因为整件事比任何人想象的都要花更长的时间，我们把她带回来，你就结束了演出。

00:35:50.780 --> 00:35:53.380
I love the what's taking so long, girl.
我喜欢花这么长时间的事情，女孩。

00:35:53.380 --> 00:35:57.579
It's sort of called it just sort of became like the theme of the show, what's taking so long?
这有点像节目的主题，什么花了这么长时间？

00:35:57.579 --> 00:35:58.579
Well, we're going to take that fucking year.
好吧，我们要度过那该死的一年。

00:35:58.579 --> 00:35:59.579
It's how long is it?
到底有多长呢？

00:35:59.579 --> 00:36:00.579
Robyn and Ted are talking.
罗宾和泰德正在谈话。

00:36:00.579 --> 00:36:04.619
Robyn and Ted are talking and she wants to, yeah, the friend wants her to come back to the corner.
罗宾和泰德正在说话，她想要，是的，朋友希望她回到角落里。

00:36:04.619 --> 00:36:05.619
What's taking so long?
什么事要花这么长时间？

00:36:05.619 --> 00:36:06.619
Because she's had a break up.
因为她已经分手了。

00:36:06.619 --> 00:36:07.619
He's had a break up and she's mad.
他分手了，她很生气。

00:36:07.619 --> 00:36:08.619
She hates all of that.
她讨厌这一切。

00:36:08.619 --> 00:36:09.619
Yeah, she hates all of that.
是的，她讨厌这一切。

00:36:09.619 --> 00:36:13.420
And she wants, she wants, she's like, where's my next round where I need to get drunker than this.
她想要，她想要，她就像，我的下一轮在哪里，我需要比这更醉。

00:36:13.420 --> 00:36:14.420
I just got dumped.
我刚刚被甩了。

00:36:14.420 --> 00:36:20.820
And that exchange, that also was so great, but you and the other moment I thought, I mean many moments I thought, hey, this might go somewhere.
那次交流也很棒，但是你和我想的另一个时刻，我的意思是很多时候我想，嘿，这可能会发生在某个地方。

00:36:20.820 --> 00:36:31.500
You and Robin up at that bar, Ted and Robin up at that bar, and the whole thing that ends with the drink in the face, which was one of the audition scenes that got both of you cast because you were magic even in an audition.
你和罗宾在那个酒吧，泰德和罗宾在那个酒吧，整个事情以喝到脸上的饮料结束，这是你们俩都被选中的试镜场景之一，因为即使在试镜中你们也很神奇。

00:36:31.500 --> 00:36:35.059
That was another moment where I was like, I remember feeling pretty good in that scene.
那是另一个时刻，我记得在那个场景中感觉很好。

00:36:35.059 --> 00:36:37.780
I mean, all over the place, I was feeling pretty good about it.
我的意思是，在所有地方，我都感觉很好。

00:36:37.780 --> 00:36:44.260
Do you remember also, it was the very last thing we shot, it was with Ranjit around the table at the bar, the funny reveal that Ranjit is with us?
你还记得吗，这是我们拍摄的最后一件事，是兰吉特在酒吧的桌子旁，有趣的是兰吉特和我们在一起？

00:36:44.260 --> 00:36:48.539
That lean in, oh my God, signal, Ranjit, what he's so good.
那一倾身，哦天啊，兰吉特，他的表现如此出色。

00:36:48.539 --> 00:36:49.539
He's so good.
他太好了。

00:36:49.539 --> 00:36:53.420
Oh, good, Marshall Manhand, he ended up doing, what, 20 episodes?
哦，很好，Marshall Manhand，他最后拍了，什么，20 集？

00:36:53.420 --> 00:36:54.420
He did a bunch.
他做了一堆。

00:36:54.420 --> 00:36:59.059
Yeah, he was an important, he was, oh man, him, him also kind of shutting out of your signal.
是的，他是一个重要人物，他是，天哪，他，他也拒绝了你的信号。

00:36:59.059 --> 00:37:00.059
That was a signal.
那是一个信号。

00:37:00.059 --> 00:37:01.059
Yeah.
是的。

00:37:01.059 --> 00:37:06.679
And I also remember they gave us real champagne to one hell of a night, to one hell of a hell of a night.
我还记得他们为我们提供了真正的香槟，度过了一个地狱般的夜晚，度过了一个地狱般的夜晚。

00:37:06.679 --> 00:37:10.500
Yeah, they gave us real champagne, which is not something I've done a lot on the set.
是的，他们给了我们真正的香槟，这不是我在片场经常做的事情。

00:37:10.500 --> 00:37:15.860
But it was, it was the last night of the shooting of the pilot and we all had a little bit of champagne.
但事实确实如此，那是飞行员拍摄的最后一晚，我们都喝了一点香槟。

00:37:15.860 --> 00:37:19.460
There was just such a warm, good feeling on set, like I think we made something good.
片场有一种温暖、美好的感觉，就像我认为我们做了一些好东西一样。

00:37:19.460 --> 00:37:21.139
That's what it felt like, right?
就是这样的感觉，对吧？

00:37:21.139 --> 00:37:22.659
It felt like we had made something good.
感觉就像我们做了一些好事。

00:37:22.659 --> 00:37:25.139
It felt like we had made the thing we set out to make.
感觉就像我们已经做出了我们打算做的事情。

00:37:25.139 --> 00:37:26.539
It really felt that way.
确实是这样的感觉。

00:37:26.539 --> 00:37:32.179
Like any endeavor in life, especially a TV pilot too, it doesn't always feel that way.
就像生活中的任何努力一样，尤其是电视飞行员，它并不总是这样的感觉。

00:37:32.179 --> 00:37:35.139
And it had this magic, there was just a magic to it.
它有这种魔力，这就是魔力。

00:37:35.139 --> 00:37:40.539
I just felt like a magic and a life to it and something that was bigger than the sum of its parts and bigger than me or you or anything.
我只是觉得它有一种魔力，有一种生命，一种比各部分总和还要大的东西，比我、你或任何东西都大。

00:37:40.539 --> 00:37:45.619
And it was like, I felt so much gratitude watching it and so much gratitude to the fans.
就像，我对观看它感到非常感激，对粉丝也非常感激。

00:37:45.619 --> 00:37:50.179
Because people found that it was a weird, It was a weird show for CBS.
因为人们发现这是一个奇怪的节目，对于哥伦比亚广播公司来说这是一个奇怪的节目。

00:37:50.179 --> 00:37:51.460
With a weird title.
带着一个奇怪的标题。

00:37:51.460 --> 00:37:52.500
Weird title.
奇怪的标题。

00:37:52.500 --> 00:38:03.780
Oh, and I mean, we tested that pilot and we're told, so after, you have this magic time shooting the pilot and then you take it and you take it to this focus groups and you put it through this somewhat corporate testing process which every pilot does.
哦，我的意思是，我们测试了那个飞行员，我们被告知，所以之后，你有一段神奇的时间拍摄飞行员，然后你把它带到这个焦点小组，然后你把它通过每个飞行员都会做的有点企业测试过程。

00:38:04.820 --> 00:38:09.139
And one of the takeaways from the testing was people hate the title.
测试的结果之一是人们讨厌这个标题。

00:38:09.139 --> 00:38:13.860
It was like, I remember the testing people being like, everyone's confused by this.
就像，我记得测试人员是这样的，每个人都对此感到困惑。

00:38:13.860 --> 00:38:16.420
You have to, I've strong recommendation to change this.
你必须这样做，我强烈建议改变这一点。

00:38:16.420 --> 00:38:22.860
And they were saying in front of the studio executives I was like, don't shut up, don't do this, can we just talk over here away from them?
他们在工作室高管面前说，我想，不要闭嘴，不要这样做，我们可以在这里远离他们说话吗？

00:38:22.860 --> 00:38:24.300
Because we did not want to change the title.
因为我们不想更改标题。

00:38:24.300 --> 00:38:27.739
The title is the thing, thank God, again, the studio and the network.
感谢上帝，标题就是重点，工作室和网络。

00:38:27.739 --> 00:38:30.940
They believed in the show, they knew the title, sold the show.
他们相信这部剧，他们知道剧名，也卖掉了这部剧。

00:38:30.940 --> 00:38:31.940
And so we didn't.
所以我们没有。

00:38:31.940 --> 00:38:33.500
But there were discussions.
但也有讨论。

00:38:33.500 --> 00:38:49.300
Is a title to confusing those time jumps I talked about, boom, boom, boom, what, what, sure enough, some people in the focus group that were, that it accepted $50 to watch a pilot last Sunday afternoon in the valley, you would wonder it in from the mall, next door or whatever.
这是一个令人困惑的标题，我谈到的那些时间跳跃，繁荣，繁荣，繁荣，什么，什么，果然，焦点小组中的一些人，上周日下午在山谷观看飞行员接受 50 美元，你会想知道它是从商场，隔壁还是其他什么地方。

00:38:49.300 --> 00:38:50.619
They were like, I don't get it.
他们说，我不明白。

00:38:50.619 --> 00:38:51.659
What's that's weird?
这有什么奇怪的？

00:38:51.659 --> 00:38:54.300
And if you were asked, did that confuse you?
如果有人问你，这会让你感到困惑吗？

00:38:54.300 --> 00:38:56.340
And you go, yeah, that is confusing.
然后你就会发现，是的，这很令人困惑。

00:38:56.340 --> 00:38:58.699
What a jump to the future, what happened?
多么跳跃到未来，发生了什么？

00:38:58.699 --> 00:39:07.460
And people, so it's very nerve-wracking when you put something this intricate and unique through that process, and you're just terrified.
人们，所以当你把如此复杂和独特的东西放在这个过程中时，你会感到非常紧张，你会感到害怕。

00:39:07.460 --> 00:39:10.219
It's going to come out the worst, but it didn't.
这将会是最糟糕的结果，但事实并非如此。

00:39:10.219 --> 00:39:11.300
It really didn't.
确实没有。

00:39:11.300 --> 00:39:25.920
When you were talking about how much had already happened by the end of Act One, I feel like because of the narrative structure, it's such a plot heavy show, such a propulsive show, so it doesn't, it can't withstand a lot of fat on it.
当你谈到第一幕结束时已经发生了多少事情时，我觉得因为叙事结构，这是一个情节如此沉重的节目，这样一个推进性的节目，所以它不，它不能承受很多脂肪。

00:39:25.920 --> 00:39:44.179
It's like everything was trimmed down to its essence, which is astonishing because my memory of doing the show while the plot is delightful and strange and always surprising, you still get so many good jokes in there, but they're character revealing and they're a plot forwarding all the dress.
就好像一切都被精简到了本质，这是令人惊讶的，因为我记得做这部剧的时候，情节是令人愉快、奇怪的，总是令人惊讶，你仍然会在里面看到很多好笑话，但它们揭示了人物的性格，它们是一个转发所有衣服的情节。

00:39:44.179 --> 00:39:45.420
They're one or the other or both.
它们是其中之一或另一个或两者兼而有之。

00:39:45.420 --> 00:39:46.260
That's exactly it.
就是这样。

00:39:46.260 --> 00:39:48.460
They're character revealing or plot forwarding or both.
它们是人物揭示或情节转发或两者兼而有之。

00:39:48.460 --> 00:39:50.139
There's almost nothing that isn't that.
几乎没有什么不是这样的。

00:39:50.139 --> 00:39:53.179
And by the way, that didn't start that way.
顺便说一句，事情并不是这样开始的。

00:39:53.179 --> 00:39:54.579
That cut of that pilot came in.
那个试播集的片段进来了。

00:39:54.579 --> 00:39:55.659
It's supposed to be 22 minutes.
应该是22分钟。

00:39:55.659 --> 00:39:57.619
I think it was 31 minutes.
我记得是 31 分钟。

00:39:57.619 --> 00:40:00.780
Overshot, we cut out whole scenes, all this fat.
过头了，我们剪掉了整个场景，所有这些脂肪。

00:40:00.780 --> 00:40:03.579
We learned so much editing that show.
我们在剪辑那个节目中学到了很多东西。

00:40:03.579 --> 00:40:05.659
It really was built in the editor room in a lot of ways.
它确实以多种方式在编辑室中构建。

00:40:05.659 --> 00:40:12.219
And when you see the edited version and you're just heartbroken most of the time because you're like, oh that's gone.
当你看到编辑后的版本时，大多数时候你都会心碎，因为你会想，哦，那已经消失了。

00:40:12.219 --> 00:40:12.787
love that.
喜欢那个。

00:40:12.787 --> 00:40:13.808
Where did that go?
那去哪儿了？

00:40:13.808 --> 00:40:15.226
No, this just got better.
不，这只是变得更好了。

00:40:15.226 --> 00:40:16.417
This just got better.
这变得更好了。

00:40:16.417 --> 00:40:19.026
Everything we cut out, we should have cut out.
我们删掉的一切，我们都应该删掉。

00:40:19.026 --> 00:40:19.526
Yeah.
是的。

00:40:19.526 --> 00:40:20.150
Everything.
一切。

00:40:20.150 --> 00:40:20.717
Oh my God.
我的天啊。

00:40:20.717 --> 00:40:21.965
It was so overwritten.
就这么被覆盖了。

00:40:21.965 --> 00:40:22.986
It came in so fat.
它进来的时候太胖了。

00:40:22.986 --> 00:40:24.404
It wasn't great at first.
一开始情况不太好。

00:40:24.404 --> 00:40:26.672
And we whittled it down on what you did.
我们根据你所做的事情进行了削减。

00:40:26.672 --> 00:40:27.172
Yeah.
是的。

00:40:26.739 --> 00:40:27.840
I have two questions.
我有两个问题。

00:40:27.840 --> 00:40:29.831
One, where the olive theory come from?
一、橄榄理论从何而来？

00:40:29.831 --> 00:40:37.115
I think that was that I think that was also a Carter Bayes gem because but but it's funny because it was sort of a Marshall and Lily thing.
我认为这也是卡特贝叶斯的瑰宝，因为但这很有趣，因为这是马歇尔和莉莉的事情。

00:40:37.115 --> 00:40:45.762
It might have been, might have been Carter's observation of like, you know, being close friends with me and seeing maybe this old married guy at age, you know, 2021.
这可能是，可能是卡特的观察，你知道，和我成为亲密朋友，也许看到这个已婚老家伙，你知道，2021 年。

00:40:45.762 --> 00:40:58.653
I mean, basically, and then even more so by the time I was 30 and like the negotiations of couple, I think it was Carter's like stealth commentary on like, you know, watching a guy in a relationship like bend a little bit and choose your battles.
我的意思是，基本上，更重要的是，当我30岁的时候，就像情侣之间的谈判一样，我认为这是卡特的秘密评论，你知道，看着一个处于恋爱关系中的男人稍微弯曲一点，选择你的战斗。

00:40:58.653 --> 00:41:02.583
And I don't know why I wouldn't want to dissuade this person of this thing.
我不知道为什么我不想劝阻这个人。

00:41:02.583 --> 00:41:11.544
And like, I think it was, I think it was Carter's clever, Clever commentary slash slight dis on maybe my my close friend watching me in a relationship with a strong woman.
就像，我认为是，我认为这是卡特的聪明的评论，对我的亲密朋友看着我与一个坚强的女人的关系进行了轻微的批评。

00:41:11.544 --> 00:41:13.011
I was like, I don't want it.
我当时想，我不想要它。

00:41:13.011 --> 00:41:17.779
I think it was like, I think it was a little bit fat, which I don't think that had any day.
我认为它有点胖，我认为这种情况不会有任何一天。

00:41:18.820 --> 00:41:29.355
The only thing in the pilot that I found that made me cringe and I think would probably, you would not write today is Barney's opening lines.
在试播集中，我发现唯一让我感到畏缩的东西，我想你今天可能不会写的是巴尼的开场白。

00:41:29.355 --> 00:41:29.855
Right.
正确的。

00:41:29.855 --> 00:41:30.355
Yeah.
是的。

00:41:30.355 --> 00:41:30.855
Yeah.
